    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The republic was restored in 1867 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#benito-juarez">Benito Juárez</a> defeated the French-backed empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#maximilian-i-holy-roman-emperor">Maximilian of Habsburg</a>.</li><li>The Revolution of 1910–1920 produced the Constitution of 1917, land reform and a ruling party that held power until 2000.</li><li>Since NAFTA in 1994 and the democratic transition of 2000, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#mexico">Mexico</a> has become a large industrial economy tied to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#united-states">United States</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The ruling party founded in 1929 changed its name twice, becoming the PRI in 1946, and won every presidential election for 71 years until Vicente Fox’s victory in 2000.</p></aside>
    </section>

